{"id":"u-b3a68a3e-9f09-45f9-aa1a-eac7587a9a2f","src":"community","title":"Beginner Program","author":"Tristan  H.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ZFWBbG-beginner-program","desc":"Progression for main lifts (5s):\nAfter finding your 5 rep max, divide that weight by 85 then multiply it by 100, that is your 1 rep max you will use.\nStart with 3x5 @80% then add 5lbs each week to every set. If it becomes too hard, only add 5lbs on 1 or 2 sets.\nProgression for secondary lifts (6-8):\nAfter doing a max effort set of 6-8 reps you use that yo gauge your set of 6-8 with one in the tank and the set with none in the tank. Once you are at 2x8, add weight.\nProgression for isolations (8-10): same as secondary lifts except that both sets have none in the tank\nIntensity: Intensity matters more than specific reps. The last set of the 5s should be 0-1 reps in the tank, if it's more, keep doing reps until you are. For 6-8s, the first set is 1 rep in reserve and the second is 0 RiR, if it isn't, keep doing reps. For 8-10s both sets are 0 RiR. Every extra 1 rep for lower body and 2 for upper means add an extra 5lbs on top of what you already would have the next week.\nCardio:\nSession 1: 5-10m jog, medium Intensity\nSession 2: 5m backwards bike, low intensity\nSession 3: Interval Sprints, High intensity","level":["Beginner"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-25T00:03:55.030Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Lateral Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"V-Handle Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":1